PURPOSE OF THIS FILE (a diff under review, D-2968/BUG-712).
This is a REVIEW UNIT, not source: it is the complete change made to pipeline/stage4_merge.py on 2026-10-12,
submitted to the R5 cross-family reviewer because the WHOLE file (152,853 chars) exceeds the reviewer's context
and the model returns HTTP 400 for it (BUG-746: a crash must never be read as a rejection, so the gate refuses
to send it). The change makes ONE line of the write path derive the content_type AUTHORSHIP from the same
computation that chose the label, instead of stamping a literal on every row.

WHY (measured). D-2938 made S4 persist the ROUTER's resolved content_type instead of the raw S2 label, but the
write site kept stamping llm_extracted_from_source on EVERY row. The next S2->S6 run would therefore write
~100 labels the DETERMINISTIC router authored (D-343/D-2747) while claiming an LLM authored them: the BUG-742
class (a provenance value TRUE of the label the row no longer carries), and the same defect shape D-2938 itself
fixed (a computed fact, discarded at the write site).

THE CLOSED VOCABULARY IT CHOOSES FROM (pipeline/schemas.py#PROVENANCE_LITERAL, a Pydantic Literal, so an
undeclared value is a ValidationError): human_verbatim | llm_extracted_from_source | llm_hypothesis |
deterministic. The function never mints a value; it selects one of the four.

REVIEW QUESTION: is this change CORRECT for that purpose and SAFE to run (no data loss, no irreversibility,
no silent failure, does it verify its own work)? Note that when the router AGREES with S2 the LLM did author
the persisted label, so the LLM stamp must (and does) stay.

